Fix xdg-desktop-portal-hyprland leaking the shm file descriptor on the two
error paths of the SHM branch of CPipewireConnection::createBuffer.

pBuffer is a std::unique_ptr<SBuffer> and SBuffer has no destructor, so
`return nullptr` after the fd has been assigned into pBuffer->fd[0] simply
abandons it:

  * ftruncate() failing on the freshly shm_open()ed fd;
  * import_wl_shm_buffer() returning nullptr.

The DMABUF branch a few dozen lines above already gets this right -- it closes
every plane fd both when zwp_linux_buffer_params_v1_create_immed fails and
when gbm_bo_get_fd_for_plane fails partway through. The SHM branch below it
just does not, which reads as an oversight rather than a deliberate
difference. The normal teardown path (destroyBuffer) closes fd[0] correctly
via planeCount, so only these two failure exits leak.

Both are error paths, so this is rare in practice; it is fixed for
consistency with the DMABUF branch and because a portal that fails to
allocate a buffer is likely to be asked again.

Found while auditing fd lifetimes in this codebase after an unrelated leak in
the input-capture portal.

Not upstreamed yet.

diff --git a/src/portals/Screencopy.cpp b/src/portals/Screencopy.cpp
index cc232e9..99c31da 100644
--- a/src/portals/Screencopy.cpp
+++ b/src/portals/Screencopy.cpp
@@ -1383,6 +1383,10 @@ std::unique_ptr<SBuffer> CPipewireConnection::createBuffer(CPipewireConnection::
 
         if (ftruncate(pBuffer->fd[0], pBuffer->size[0]) < 0) {
             Debug::log(ERR, "[screencopy] ftruncate failed");
+            // SBuffer has no destructor, so returning here abandons the fd --
+            // the DMABUF branch above already closes its fds on the equivalent
+            // failures, this one did not.
+            close(pBuffer->fd[0]);
             return nullptr;
         }
 
@@ -1390,6 +1394,7 @@ std::unique_ptr<SBuffer> CPipewireConnection::createBuffer(CPipewireConnection::
                                                  pStream->pSession->sharingData.frameInfoSHM.h, pStream->pSession->sharingData.frameInfoSHM.stride);
         if (!pBuffer->wlBuffer) {
             Debug::log(ERR, "[screencopy] import_wl_shm_buffer failed");
+            close(pBuffer->fd[0]);
             return nullptr;
         }
     }
